1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,278
To make a voltmeter that reads up to V, connect a large resistance R, the multiplier, in series.

2
00:00:07,278 --> 00:00:16,523
Choose it so that exactly I g flows when the full voltage V is across the meter: V equals I g times G plus R.

3
00:00:16,523 --> 00:00:20,403
So R equals V over I g, minus G.

